    <string name="info_title">How clipboard access works</string>
    <string name="info_message">ClipboardPro keeps your history on this device only. It needs no account and no internet.\n\nWhat it can capture depends on your Android version:\n\n• Android 9 and below: a background service can watch the clipboard.\n\n• Android 10 and above: Android only lets the app in the foreground (or the active keyboard) read the clipboard. ClipboardPro saves what you copied when you open it, while it is on screen, from the “Save clipboard” notification button or app shortcut, and through Share or Select text → Save to ClipboardPro.\n\n• Android 12 and above may show a small notice when an app reads the clipboard.\n\nSo copies made while the app is closed can’t always be captured. ClipboardPro never promises unrestricted automatic tracking.</string>
